## Data Storage

JavaScript arrays and objects are used to store
client, project, document, ticket, invoice and message data.

Local Storage is used to preserve changes in the browser.

## How to Run

1. Download the project files.
2. Open the project folder in VS Code.
3. Make sure all four files are in the same folder.
4. Open index.html in your browser.
5. Login using the demo credentials.

## Learning Outcomes

- Understanding HTML page structure.
- Creating responsive layouts using CSS.
- Implementing JavaScript functionality.
- Working with arrays and objects.
- Implementing CRUD operations.
- Using browser Local Storage.
- Creating client and admin interfaces.
- Building interactive dashboards.

## Limitations

This is a frontend-only demonstration project.
Authentication is simulated and is not suitable for production.
Uploaded documents are represented by metadata, and demo
downloads are generated locally. A backend is required for
secure authentication, real file storage and shared data.

## Conclusion

The Client Portal System provides an organized platform
for client management and self-service. The project
demonstrates frontend development skills using HTML,
CSS and JavaScript.